course: dictionary
lesson: 15955
title: The word untagged
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: The word untagged is made of two parts. The start, un-, means not. The middle, tag, means a label or a marker. So untagged means not tagged, or without a tag. When you meet a word with un- at the start, ask: what is the word without the un-?
explain: «The suitcase at the airport was untagged, so nobody knew whose it was.» The clue is the word nobody knew whose it was. A bag with no label cannot show its owner, so untagged means without a label.
explain: The same word can be used for animals, photos and games. Read the sentence around it, and it will tell you which kind of tag is missing.
fact: Untagged means without a tag or label.
fact: The prefix un- means not, so untagged means not tagged.
fact: In computing, an untagged photo or post has no name linked to it.
fact: In science, an untagged animal has not been fitted with a tag so that scientists can follow it.
fact: In the game of tag, an untagged player has not been caught.
exercise: «The suitcase at the airport was untagged, so nobody knew whose it was.» What does untagged mean? | Packed and ready to fly | Opened and empty | *Without a tag or label | Very heavy
exercise: «The scientists could not follow the shark, because it was untagged.» Why could they not follow it? | *It had no tag to track it | It was too fast to see | It was asleep | It was hungry
exercise: The prefix un- in untagged means what? | Again | *Not | Very | Before
test: In the playground game, Sam shouted, «You are untagged, so run!» What does untagged mean in this game? | *Not caught yet | Asleep | Caught and out | Wearing a badge
test: «Please leave my photo untagged, so my name does not show.» Why would someone say this? | Because they want more people to see their name | Because the photo is too dark | *Because they want to keep their name private | Because they lost their phone
exam: A science team wanted to follow the turtles, but three of them had no tracking tag. Which word best describes those three turtles? | Ancient | Luminous | Hungry | *Untagged
